node_modules/
dist/
.vitest/
*.log
.DS_Store
# GitHub rejects raw files over 100 MB without LFS, and ner.onnx is 111 MB. The smaller
# weights predate this rule and are tracked; ner.onnx is not, so a fresh clone gets some
# of the models and not others.
#
# That used to be silent, which is the part that mattered: the bundle built, loaded, and
# failed in the offscreen document several layers from the cause. It is not silent now --
# extension/models/manifest.json records every weight with its size, digest, licence and
# provenance, and extension/build.mjs refuses to build when one is absent or is not the
# file that was measured. `python scripts/fetch-models.py` is the way back.
extension/models/*.onnx
# Server-side vLLM weights, fetched for offline deployment. model.safetensors is 943 MB --
# far past GitHub's 100 MB limit -- and like the .onnx weights above it is provenance, not
# source. server/OFFLINE.md documents how to re-fetch. The HF download cache under it is
# pure build cruft.
server/models/
# Generated by eval/harness.py. The report is a build artefact of a specific run on a
# specific machine, and a committed one is a number nobody can reproduce or date.
eval/report/*.json
eval/report/*.html
eval/report/runs*/
# Same reasoning for the scenario suite and the live-site runs: screenshots and per-run
# JSON are evidence of one run on one machine, not source.
eval/report/scenarios/
eval/report/live/
eval/report/build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# Per-machine Claude Code permissions -- local to this checkout, not shared config.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Windows / editor cruft.
Thumbs.db
*.tmp
.idea/
.vscode/
